Australian Product Guide — Brand Fidelity v32.4 certified presentation release
Release date: 2026-08-18
Status: CURRENT RELEASE CANDIDATE / PRODUCTION CERTIFICATION REQUIRED AFTER MERGE
Production source: GitHub main via Vercel
Canonical production domain: https://australianproductguide.au

Current platform: the underlying APG application/data capability remains the maintained priority-commerce / Decision Intelligence v4.1 / Evidence & Commerce Depth v27 / Trust Infrastructure v28 / Amazon Conversion v29 stack, with Premium Brand v30, Premium Theme v31.1 and Brand Fidelity v32.4 forming the controlling presentation system once this release is merged and exact-Production certified. The architecture remains lightweight SSR-first Node with progressive enhancement. v32.4 changes presentation and release controls only; it does not change product-fit logic, catalogue data, retailer ranking, affiliate weighting, account/auth behaviour, analytics consent or privacy controls.

Brand-fidelity truth: the owner-approved APG brand board is implemented as a coherent production identity rather than an approximate A-shaped logo. The current mark uses the traced four-part APG geometry and first-party responsive assets for primary horizontal, compact, APG monogram, standalone symbol, white, monochrome, favicon, app-icon and social applications. Desktop uses the full Australian Product Guide lock-up. Standard tablet/mobile widths use the APG symbol/monogram relationship, with the monogram P kept white on navy so the complete APG mark remains legible.

Colour-system truth: the controlling palette is APG Blue #2563EB, APG Navy #0F172A, APG Teal #06B6D4, APG Green #10B981, Light Grey #F1F5F9 and Slate #64748B, supported by white and accessible light/dark text tokens. Navy is used for institutional authority and deep surfaces; blue is the primary action colour; teal/green remain selective accents; white/light grey provide breathing space. Dark surfaces use white or sufficiently light foreground text rather than low-contrast navy/grey combinations.

Maintained-research highlight: the successful historical yellow treatment was recovered from APG source history rather than guessed. The MAINTAINED AUSTRALIAN RESEARCH band uses #FFD65B → #F4BB45 → #F2B348, with #E0A630/#D89C24 border tones and dark foreground treatment. The main proof text remains based on the recovered #082735 family and the independence copy is explicitly #2B4B56 at strong weight. Yellow remains a strategic trust accent rather than a primary site colour. The product/category/brand values remain data-driven from the authoritative maintained catalogue rather than hard-coded release numbers.

Scout and proof clearance: Scout remains APG's decision-assistance product and uses the APG Blue + white master symbol consistently after JavaScript initialisation. v32.2 introduced the runtime identity guard that prevents the legacy mascot overwriting the approved APG mark. v32.3 makes the fixed desktop launcher a compact 58px APG-symbol control, preserving accessible launcher labelling while preventing the floating control from obscuring the yellow research independence statement. Scout decision logic, structured-session continuity and zero-commercial-weight recommendation controls are unchanged.

Mobile navigation reconciliation: manual review of the exact v32.3 Production screenshot matrix identified one final hierarchy defect in the open tablet/mobile menu: Decision Lab could appear twice while the intended Ask Scout shortcut was displaced or visually mislabelled after later client enhancement. v32.4 explicitly reconciles that runtime state to exactly one primary Decision Lab action followed immediately by exactly one differentiated Ask Scout action, then the existing Popular products, Research & compare and Trust & transparency accordion groups. A MutationObserver maintains that hierarchy if earlier client code updates the menu after load. This is a presentation-only correction.

Catalogue and commerce truth: catalogue, retailer, Amazon and recommendation facts are verified from the live observability contract during exact-Production certification rather than copied into the interface as release constants. The maintained-research banner reads those live product/category/brand sources. Affiliate participation, retailer availability and commission contribute zero recommendation points.

Imagery truth: the governed registry continues to distinguish authorised external exact-model photography from first-party/category-correct authored decision visuals. APG does not scrape Amazon product pages, reverse-engineer image URLs, fabricate real-product photography or claim third-party imagery rights it does not hold. Authorised genuine-product image delivery remains a separate ingestion task where rights/delivery are not available.

Responsive and accessibility truth: the final visual system is certified separately across desktop, tablet and mobile. It strengthens dark/light surface contrast, keeps the responsive APG monogram readable, preserves the distinctive yellow proof band, fixes yellow-band independence-copy contrast, prevents true document-width overflow, retains readable footer/trust typography, keeps product/search/category/comparison/Decision Lab/My APG/Scout surfaces visually coherent, and now regression-gates the intended mobile Decision Lab/Ask Scout hierarchy. Legitimate internally scrollable comparison/research content is not incorrectly treated as page overflow.

Implementation history: PR #79 established the v32.2 board-faithful identity and mobile/Scout corrections. PR #81 introduced v32.3 after screenshot review found residual yellow-proof contrast and Scout-clearance defects. The v32.3 exact Production visual matrix then exposed the final mobile-menu duplicate/displacement issue. v32.4 is the final screenshot-led reconciliation and includes the mobile-menu runtime guard plus expanded exact-Production assertions for one Decision Lab, one Ask Scout, correct order, differentiated Scout styling, yellow proof contrast, Scout clearance, responsive brand fidelity, dark-surface readability, Decision Lab SSR results and document-width integrity.

Release verification requirement: this file is intentionally included in the same v32.4 implementation PR so the final merged GitHub main SHA can remain the exact SHA that Vercel Production and the visual certification workflows certify. Completion requires Vercel READY on the canonical domain, APG v27 Visual Certification success, APG v32 Brand Visual Certification success on that exact final SHA, publication of the final screenshot artefact, manual inspection of the refreshed mobile-menu render, and a clear post-release Vercel error/fatal log window.

Remaining external gaps: lawful genuine-product photography ingestion remains incomplete until an authorised delivery/right basis exists. Hosted Supabase Auth settings outside the connected writable surface, including any previously identified leaked-password-protection setting unless subsequently verified, remain separate owner/admin configuration work. Formal trade mark clearance/registration is not claimed by this release.
